   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C7} = 1024$
   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C8} = 2736$
   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C9} = 1129$
   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C10} = 676$
   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C11} = 2631$
   - $\sum_{s} x_{s,C12} = 31$

2. **Supply capacity at each supply center:**

   $$
   \sum_{c \in C} x_{s,c} \leq u_s \qquad \forall s \in S
   $$

   Explicitly:
   - $\sum_{c} x_{S1,c} \leq 58$
   - $\sum_{c} x_{S2,c} \leq 32$
   - $\sum_{c} x_{S3,c} \leq 6161$
