   - $\sum_{c} x_{S11,c} \leq 7081$
   - $\sum_{c} x_{S12,c} \leq 948$

3. **Nonnegativity:**

   $$
   x_{s,c} \geq 0 \qquad \forall s \in S,\, c \in C
   $$

**Summary of Variables and Parameters:**

- $x_{s,c}$: units shipped from supply center $s$ to customer group $c$ (continuous, $\geq 0$)
- $t_{s,c}$: transportation cost per unit (see table above)
- $d_c$: demand for customer $c$ (see above)
- $u_s$: supply capacity at $s$ (see above)

**Complete Model:**

$$
\begin{align*}
\min_{x_{s,c} \geq 0} \quad & \sum_{s \in S} \sum_{c \in C} t_{s,c} \cdot x_{s,c} \\
\text{s.t.} \quad
& \sum_{s \in S} x_{s,c} = d_c \qquad \forall c \in C \\
& \sum_{c \in C} x_{s,c} \leq u_s \qquad \forall s \in S \\
& x_{s,c} \geq 0 \qquad \forall s \in S,\, c \in C \\
\end{align*}
$$

